{"file":"Runpod-1.2.0-v2.zip","bytes":417717,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"runpod","description":"Official Runpod agent skills and MCP server — run Runpod tasks (pods, serverless, templates, volumes) with runpodctl and flash, plus conceptual guidance and worked golden paths.","version":"1.2.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/runpod/runpod-plugins-official","homepage":"https://github.com/runpod/runpod-plugins-official","keywords":["runpod","gpu","serverless","pods","mcp","runpodctl","flash","infrastructure"]},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"runpod","description":"Official Runpod agent skills and MCP server — run Runpod tasks (pods, serverless, templates, volumes) with runpodctl and flash, plus conceptual guidance and worked golden paths.","version":"1.2.0","homepage":"https://github.com/runpod/runpod-plugins-official/tree/main/plugins/runpod","keywords":["runpod","gpu","serverless","pods","mcp","runpodctl","flash","infrastructure"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/companion-clis/SKILL.md","name":"companion-clis","description":"Companion CLIs for Runpod workflows — HuggingFace, GitHub, Docker, and AWS. Use the ComfyUI model-repair guide in runpod-templates instead when an imported ComfyUI workflow lacks model download metadata.","headings":["Companion CLIs","Windows: Install WSL2 First","HuggingFace CLI","GitHub CLI","Docker","AWS CLI"],"name_hint":"companion · clis","description_zh":"提供 Runpod 工作流配套的 HuggingFace、GitHub、Docker 和 AWS 命令行工具使用说明；导入 ComfyUI 工作流缺少模型下载元数据时改用模板技能的模型修复指南。"},{"path":"skills/flash/SKILL.md","name":"flash","description":"runpod-flash — code-first serverless: write Python locally, run it on remote Runpod GPUs/CPUs with `flash dev` (hot-reload + live worker logs), then `flash deploy`. Use for @Endpoint/@remote functions, resource config, and debugging flash deployments. For CLI-only infra management use runpodctl or runpod-mcp.","headings":["Runpod Flash","Dev vs Deploy","Autonomous Dev Loop","Endpoint: Three Modes","Mode 1: Your Code (Queue-Based Decorator)","Mode 2: Your Code (Load-Balanced Routes)","Mode 3: External Image (Client)","LB-style","QB-style","How Mode Is Determined","When to use `image=` (custom container) vs your own code","Gotchas","Resources"],"name_hint":"flash","description_zh":"使用 runpod-flash 在本地编写 Python，以 flash dev 在远程 Runpod GPU 或 CPU 上热更新运行并查看日志，再用 flash deploy 部署；涵盖 Endpoint、remote 函数、资源配置和故障排查，纯基础设施管理另用专用工具。"},{"path":"skills/runpod-mcp/SKILL.md","name":"runpod-mcp","description":"Manage Runpod infrastructure — pods, serverless endpoints, jobs, templates, network volumes, container-registry auth, GPU/CPU catalog, and billing — via the Runpod MCP server's structured tool calls. Use when the Runpod MCP tools (create-pod, list-endpoints, …) are connected in this session, or to connect them (hosted OAuth or local npx). Prefer this over runpodctl for plain infra CRUD when MCP is available; use runpodctl for the terminal, file transfer, or SSH setup.","headings":["Runpod MCP","Connect","→ serverInfo.version e.g. \"3.0.0 [RUNPOD_REST_VERSION=v2]\"  (verified 2026-07-29)","Tool surface","Use MCP vs runpodctl","Source & docs"],"name_hint":"runpod · mcp","description_zh":"通过 Runpod MCP 结构化工具管理 Pod、无服务器端点、任务、模板、网络卷、镜像仓库认证、GPU/CPU 目录和计费，并通过托管 OAuth 或本地 npx 连接；有 MCP 时优先用于普通增删改查，终端、文件传输和 SSH 使用 runpodctl。"},{"path":"skills/runpod-migrate/SKILL.md","name":"runpod-migrate","description":"Migrate a codebase from the Runpod GraphQL API or REST v1 to REST v2 — inventory which parts use which API version, rewrite the call sites, flag breaking changes, and verify. Use when someone asks to move to v2, asks what v2 would change, or asks which Runpod API their code is on. For managing infrastructure rather than migrating code, use runpod-mcp or runpodctl.","headings":["Migrate to Runpod REST v2","Before you touch any code","The workflow","1. Inventory — never migrate what you have not counted","1. Claude Code plugin installs expose the plugin root:","2. Otherwise substitute the directory you loaded this SKILL.md from — you know it:","3. Last resort, search the usual install roots:","2. Brief the breaking changes — before the diff, not after","3. Plan, split into required vs cleanup","4. Migrate, one file per commit","5. Verify against the live API","6. Summarize — this is the artifact they will actually read","Required for the migration","Cleanup enabled by v2","Behavior changes to watch","Still on GraphQL (no v2 equivalent)","Unlocks: what you can build now","Ground truth: check the spec yourself"],"name_hint":"runpod · migrate","description_zh":"将代码从 Runpod GraphQL 或 REST v1 迁移到 REST v2，调查调用版本、改写调用点、标记破坏性变化并核验；基础设施管理使用 MCP 或 runpodctl。"},{"path":"skills/runpod-templates/SKILL.md","name":"runpod-templates","description":"Runpod''s official prebuilt pod templates (ComfyUI, PyTorch, and others): what each image ships, which ports and paths it uses, how to pick one, how to pin a version, and what is missing on first boot. Use when a task says \"run <X> on a pod\" and an official template already covers it, instead of building an image — and when a user needs help with or wants to fix something about a Runpod template they are already running (won''t boot, can''t reach the UI, missing models, wrong CUDA line, broken ComfyUI workflow metadata on imported workflows): start here and route onward. Deploy with runpodctl or runpod-mcp; end-to-end walkthroughs live in the runpod router''s golden paths.","headings":["Official Runpod templates","Terms — \"template\" vs the Hub","What \"official\" means, and how to find them","REST v2 has no template search — only slices you filter yourself","The templates","How to use a template reference","Routing onward — this skill is the hub, not the destination"],"name_hint":"runpod · templates","description_zh":"解释 Runpod 官方预构建 Pod 模板的内容、端口、路径、选型、版本固定及首次启动缺项，覆盖 ComfyUI、PyTorch 等；也排查无法启动、UI 不通、缺模型、CUDA 或导入工作流元数据问题，部署交由 runpodctl 或 MCP。"},{"path":"skills/runpod-usage/SKILL.md","name":"runpod-usage","description":"How Runpod works and how to work it — pods vs serverless, GPU/VRAM selection, storage, building a container, networking, plus the agentic pod development loop (provision → ssh-exec → set up → poll readiness) and on-pod install hygiene (uv/apt). Use to answer \"how does X work\", \"which GPU\", \"how do I build a container\", or \"how do I stand up a workload on a pod\". Guidance, not a tool — execute with runpodctl, runpod-mcp, or flash.","headings":["Runpod usage (concepts)"],"name_hint":"runpod · usage","description_zh":"解释 Runpod Pod 与无服务器服务、GPU 和显存选型、存储、容器构建及网络，并提供创建、SSH 执行、配置、就绪轮询的 Pod 开发流程和 uv、apt 安装规范；属于指导，实际操作交由 CLI、MCP 或 flash。"},{"path":"skills/runpod/SKILL.md","name":"runpod","description":"Start here for any Runpod task — running GPU/CPU pods, deploying serverless endpoints, templates, network volumes, building images, or understanding how Runpod works. Routes to the right skill (runpod-mcp, runpodctl, flash, companion-clis, runpod-usage, runpod-templates, runpod-migrate) and indexes two dozen live-verified end-to-end examples (golden paths) — use it when the lane is unclear, and for any multi-step or provisioning task even when it is not.","headings":["Runpod (router)","The lanes","These skills are a snapshot; the tools are the source of truth","First run — check auth before the first infra action","How to route","runpod-mcp vs runpodctl (the overlap)","Deploying a workload (the golden loop)","Worked examples (golden paths)","Multi-lane tasks","Auth"],"name_hint":"runpod","description_zh":"作为 Runpod 任务入口，为 GPU/CPU Pod、无服务器端点、模板、网络卷、镜像和平台使用问题选择专用技能；原说明索引了约二十四条已实时验证的端到端示例，适用于路线不明或多步骤资源配置。"},{"path":"skills/runpodctl/SKILL.md","name":"runpodctl","description":"Runpod CLI for managing GPU/CPU workloads from the terminal — pods, serverless endpoints, templates, network volumes, Hub deploys, models, SSH, and file transfer (send/receive). Use for terminal/CI/scripting, Hub browse/deploy, SSH setup, `doctor`, or when the Runpod MCP tools are not connected. For structured tool calls in an MCP-enabled session, prefer runpod-mcp.","headings":["Runpodctl","Install","Quick start","Live Help Is Authoritative","Output & errors","Decision Rules","Serverless facts (context, not rules)","Commands","Pods","Hub","Serverless (alias: sls)","Templates (alias: tpl)","Network Volumes (alias: nv)","Models (Model Repository)","Info & SSH","File Transfer","Utilities","URLs"],"name_hint":"runpodctl","description_zh":"通过 Runpod CLI 在终端、CI 或脚本管理 GPU/CPU Pod、端点、模板、网络卷、Hub 部署、模型、SSH 和文件传输，支持 doctor；MCP 已连接时结构化调用优先使用 MCP。"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/migrate.md","name":"migrate","description":"Migrate this codebase from the Runpod GraphQL API or REST v1 to REST v2 — inventory, rewrite, verify.","headings":[]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Runpod","Which skill?","The development loop","Golden paths — check these first","Getting a model onto a worker","Setup","Usage","URLs","Structure","License"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/README.md","headings":["Golden paths","Before you run any path (shared prerequisites)","Layout","Table of contents","How to use these","Status legend","Cross-cutting requirements (every path)"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/02-comfyui-pod/README.md","headings":["Golden path 02 — ComfyUI server on a pod + access URL","Which variant should I use?","Variants","Acceptance criteria (shared)","Cross-cutting gotchas (shared)","Cost & cleanup (shared)"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/25-bake-vs-mount/README.md","headings":["Golden path 25 — bake into the image vs mount a network volume","Prerequisites","The mental model","The image","Build + push","Provision a **standard** network volume + attach it to a CPU pod","standard-tier volume (high-performance tier is console / v2-REST only — see GP21)","→ volume id, e.g. fgw5d0q0sd","pod must be in the SAME data center as the volume; volume mounts at /workspace","Inspect the two side by side","Run this on the pod (fill -i/host/port from the ssh_command that ssh info printed) —","it writes to the volume AND compares filesystems:","Tear down","What this proves"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/03-whisper-endpoint/README.md","headings":["Golden path 03 — Whisper endpoint (audio → text)","Lane choice (why serverless, and why Hub is the default)","Which variant should I use?","Variants","Input & output schema (shared)","Cross-cutting gotchas (shared)","Cost & cleanup (shared)","flash apps can also be removed with: flash app delete <app-name>"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/22-minimal-pod-image/README.md","headings":["Golden path 22 — minimal **pod** image (and don't kill SSH)","Prerequisites","The image","Build + push (x86_64 Linux — emulated on Apple Silicon)","Make sure your SSH key is on the account (so it lands in `PUBLIC_KEY`)","no key yet? generate one first:  ssh-keygen -t ed25519","Launch (CPU pod — cheapest; this workload needs no GPU)","→ pod id, e.g. m9e1ow8y6pwm2x ; costPerHr ~0.06","Verify SSH works (the whole point)","paste the `ssh_command` field verbatim — it includes the right `-i <key>` path","(the exact key filename varies per account; don't hardcode it), e.g.:","ssh -i <key-from-ssh-info> root@<ip> -p <port>","Tear down","What this proves"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/23-minimal-queue-image/README.md","headings":["Golden path 23 — minimal serverless **queue** image","Prerequisites","The image","Build + push","Deploy (CPU — cheapest; this handler needs no GPU)","1. serverless template pointing at the image","→ returns a template id, e.g. jvhybsopo4","2. CPU endpoint from that template (min workers 0, scales to zero when idle)","→ returns an endpoint id, e.g. b5nopviq75s0cn","Invoke","Uses $RUNPOD_API_KEY (the recommended setup); falls back to runpodctl's config.toml.","Test locally first (no spend)","--platform linux/amd64 because the image is amd64 (emulated on Apple Silicon)","Tear down","What this proves"]},{"path":"skills/runpod/golden-paths/09-custom-serverless-dev-loop/README.md","headings":["Golden path 09 — custom serverless the hard way (iterate in a pod, then flip to serverless)","When to use this — the escape hatch","The core idea: one handler, two modes","The template (vendored in [`template/`](template/))","Walkthrough — the repeatable loop","1. Provision a dev pod (interactive, from an official base)","once ready, read ip / port / key from `ssh info` into shell vars (SSH-over-TCP form, golden path 06);","every ssh/scp below uses \"$IP\"/\"$PORT\"/\"$KEY\":","2. Iterate the handler IN the pod (`python handler.py` loop)","copy the four template files up to /app on the pod (scp uses -P for the port, ssh uses -p):","then install deps + run the pod-mode self-test over SSH (no image rebuild per change):","faster-whisper installs clean; runpod needs two extra pip flags on this base (see below)","3. Bake it into an image and build for amd64","4. Parity check — run `python handler.py` in *your* image on a clean `/app`","5. Flip to serverless — same image, one env var","1. serverless template with the image + the env that flips the mode (--env takes JSON)","2. endpoint from that template (gpu-id, not gpu-type; workers-min 0 = scale-to-zero)","6. Verify with a real request — \"up\" ≠ \"ready\"","→ {\"id\":\"<job-id>\",\"status\":\"IN_QUEUE\"}   then poll /status/<job-id> until COMPLETED","Heavy things → network volume (don't bake giant weights)","Verify it works (all three passed live, 2026-07-10)","Gotchas this path will hit","Cost & cleanup","Relation to the other paths","Skill facts confirmed / folded back (live run 2026-07-10)"]}],"mcp_servers":["runpod"],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".codex-plugin/plugin.json",".mcp.json","CHANGELOG.md","README.md","commands/migrate.md","gemini-extension.json","skills/companion-clis/SKILL.md","skills/companion-clis/reference/aws-setup.md","skills/companion-clis/reference/aws.md","skills/companion-clis/reference/docker-setup.md",